1
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:12,064
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:21,363
When Musa(موسى) passed away; the leadership was handed down to Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون);

3
00:00:22,249 --> 00:00:26,956
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) who is mentioned in Qur'an as a servant;

4
00:00:27,329 --> 00:00:28,022
اَفَتَاهُ’

5
00:00:29,135 --> 00:00:30,789
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِفَتَاهُ

6
00:00:32,042 --> 00:00:34,453
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) was a servant with Musa(موسى).

7
00:00:35,846 --> 00:00:42,164
Being a servant with Musa(موسى), he was close to the revelation; close to the teacher,

8
00:00:43,464 --> 00:00:47,770
and he was a righteous student of this teacher.

9
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:56,315
So when Musaعليه السلام passed away; the leadership was handed down to, Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون),

10
00:00:56,608 --> 00:00:58,495
and Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) is Nabi(نَبِي);

11
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:03,504
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) is a Nabi(نَبِي), but he is not mentioned in Qur'an;

12
00:01:04,317 --> 00:01:07,217
he is mentioned in the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

13
00:01:07,851 --> 00:01:13,817
The name of Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) is not in Qur'an, but it is from Hadith(حديث), and it is in the Sahih Hadith(صحيح حديث).

14
00:01:14,777 --> 00:01:17,483
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون), in English; Joshua.

15
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:22,406
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) became the leader of the children of Israel(اسرائيل).

16
00:01:23,506 --> 00:01:32,966
The children of Israel(اسرائيل) were delivered to the Holy Land, and they were victorious; under his leadership.

17
00:01:34,026 --> 00:01:37,879
 this did not happen with Musaعليه السلام and it did not happen with Haroon(هارون).

18
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:40,719
Rather, it happened in the time of Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون).

19
00:01:41,299 --> 00:01:45,779
Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون); they passed away when Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were in the wilderness.

20
00:01:47,046 --> 00:01:54,465
Rasool Allah ﷺ tells us a clue of the reason, why this victory was delayed.

21
00:01:54,891 --> 00:02:02,383
The children of Israel(اسرائيل) who came out from Egypt, were raised up in servitude and slavery.

22
00:02:03,149 --> 00:02:08,042
So, they were weak, and they were not fit for victory.

23
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:16,801
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them stay in the wilderness for 40 years.

24
00:02:17,781 --> 00:02:21,230
Until, all of that generation passed away,

25
00:02:22,123 --> 00:02:30,680
and a new generation who was raised up in freedom under the leadership and the teaching of Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون);

26
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:36,153
These are the ones who were given the victory to enter Jerusalem.

27
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:41,566
The ones who were raised up by Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون) in a free environment.

28
00:02:42,093 --> 00:02:47,819
Because, the environment in Egypt was not suitable to raise up a generation of victory.

29
00:02:50,632 --> 00:02:52,112
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

30
00:02:52,152 --> 00:02:56,072
لم یبقی معه احد ممن عبدالعجل

31
00:02:56,185 --> 00:03:02,954
Rasool Ullah says; None of the ones; who worship the calf, entered into Jerusalem.

32
00:03:03,247 --> 00:03:09,092
All of that old generation who worshipped the calf; were dead,

33
00:03:09,726 --> 00:03:21,005
a new generation was raised up in the desert; in that harsh environment; under the teachings of Torah(تورة); under the hands of Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون);

34
00:03:21,565 --> 00:03:24,803
these are the ones who were qualified for leadership.

35
00:03:24,923 --> 00:03:26,250
We learned something interesting for them.

36
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:32,061
There's no doubt; that Musa(موسى) is the greatest Nabi(نَبِي) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

37
00:03:33,094 --> 00:03:35,768
How come did the victory happened in the time of Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون)?

38
00:03:37,448 --> 00:03:39,752
And it tells us, there is not enough to have a leader.

39
00:03:40,812 --> 00:03:48,504
Musa(موسى); is the best that Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) have seen, and he is the founder of this nation.

40
00:03:49,238 --> 00:03:53,796
Nevertheless, victory did not happen on his hands even though he desired it so greatly.

41
00:03:54,169 --> 00:03:56,049
He wanted to enter into the Holy Land.

42
00:03:56,256 --> 00:04:02,072
And we know how much he desired that, that when the angel of death came to take his soul, he hit him,

43
00:04:03,012 --> 00:04:08,457
and then; when he knew that this is his appointed time, he said, I will die now

44
00:04:08,497 --> 00:04:12,651
but, oh Allah! Make me die as close to Jerusalem as possible.

45
00:04:12,671 --> 00:04:13,372
رمي حجر

46
00:04:13,452 --> 00:04:14,346
Throw of a stone.

47
00:04:14,966 --> 00:04:20,232
He said; If I cannot enter into Jerusalem alive, at least bury me as close as possible to Jerusalem.

48
00:04:20,705 --> 00:04:26,784
But that did not happen in the time of Musa(موسى), because the generation which were with Musa(موسى) did not deserve it.

49
00:04:27,984 --> 00:04:31,490
So now when we keep on thinking that, I mean; we're waiting for Al-Mahdi(ال مهدى);

50
00:04:31,917 --> 00:04:33,303
everyone is waiting for Al-Mahdi(المهدى).

51
00:04:33,757 --> 00:04:37,247
It's not an issue of a Al-Mahdi(المهدى); If you're not ready; Al-Mahdi(المهدى) cannot do you anything.

52
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:40,426
The generation has to be ready and prepared for victory.

53
00:04:40,506 --> 00:04:43,799
It's not an issue of a leader; the generation have to be ready and prepared.

54
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:50,165
And that's why, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were not able to enter into Jerusalem until, there was a suitable generation for victory.

55
00:04:50,332 --> 00:04:53,435
And these are the ones who entered with Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون),

56
00:04:53,581 --> 00:04:57,921
and we will see the miracle which Allahسُبحانه وتعالى performed for them.

57
00:04:58,248 --> 00:05:02,618
When you have Allah on your side; don't worry! Allah will do everything for you.

58
00:05:03,364 --> 00:05:06,914
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) was fighting with Al-Jababirah(الجبابره).

59
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:11,684
Al-Jababirah(الجبابره) were the people who were living in Jerusalem.

60
00:05:11,824 --> 00:05:14,420
They were giants, powerful, tyrants.

61
00:05:15,227 --> 00:05:18,067
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) led the children of Israel(اسرائيل) in that battle.

62
00:05:18,953 --> 00:05:21,339
The fighting was furious.

63
00:05:21,685 --> 00:05:23,072
The sun was about to set.

64
00:05:23,612 --> 00:05:28,541
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) knew, that he would need more time; it's not enough for him.

65
00:05:28,854 --> 00:05:33,107
He cannot win, except if the day is longer.

66
00:05:33,941 --> 00:05:37,890
If they wait for the next day, the army will regroup and attack again.

67
00:05:38,403 --> 00:05:39,663
So he needs the more time.

68
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:43,055
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) pointed to the sun and said;

69
00:05:44,015 --> 00:05:45,549
أنت مأمورةٌ وأنا مأمورٌ

70
00:05:46,115 --> 00:05:48,581
You are receiving orders, and I'm receiving orders.

71
00:05:48,841 --> 00:05:53,475
Both of us are receiving orders from Allah; so stop!

72
00:05:54,015 --> 00:05:55,428
He told the sun stop.

73
00:05:55,751 --> 00:05:59,790
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made the sun stop for Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون).

74
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:04,790
Until he finished, and destroyed the enemy, then the sun started moving again.

75
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:09,336
If you have Allahسُبحانه وتعالى on your side; don't worry! Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will take care of you.

76
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:16,368
It's not a matter of numbers, or weapons, or air force, or artillery, or battalions.

77
00:06:16,502 --> 00:06:19,137
If you have Allah with you; Allah will help you.

78
00:06:20,017 --> 00:06:22,391
He pointed to the sun; to stop! It stopped.

79
00:06:23,684 --> 00:06:25,787
And this Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

80
00:06:26,214 --> 00:06:28,247
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

81
00:06:28,334 --> 00:06:30,361
غزا نبيٌّ من الأنبياءِ ،

82
00:06:30,608 --> 00:06:35,788
فقال لقومِه : لا يتبعُني رجلٌ قد ملك بُضعَ امرأةٍ ،

83
00:06:36,254 --> 00:06:40,012
وهو يُريدُ أن يبنيَ بها ولم يبْنِ

84
00:06:40,586 --> 00:06:46,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; One of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) went into war, and he told his army;

85
00:06:46,392 --> 00:06:54,791
if any one of you just got married, you did not sleep with your wife yet, and you want to; then don't come with me.

86
00:06:56,611 --> 00:06:57,604
And then he said;

87
00:06:58,264 --> 00:07:03,693
ولا آخرُ قد بنَى بنيانًا ولمَّا يرفَعْ سقفَها

88
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:10,473
And if anybody is building a house, and he did not build the roof yet, then don't come with me.

89
00:07:11,166 --> 00:07:14,053
What is the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) telling his people;

90
00:07:14,513 --> 00:07:18,506
If you got married to a woman, and you did not sleep with her yet, don't come with me.

91
00:07:18,746 --> 00:07:22,046
If you are building a house, and you did not build the roof yet, don't come with me.

92
00:07:22,199 --> 00:07:29,566
If you have bought some pregnant goats or pregnant camels, and you're waiting for them to deliver, don't come with me.

93
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:36,275
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) does not want anybody to come with him; if their hearts are attached to something else.

94
00:07:37,642 --> 00:07:39,795
If your heart is with your wife, don't come with me.

95
00:07:40,761 --> 00:07:43,241
If your heart is with your house, don't come with me.

96
00:07:43,415 --> 00:07:47,578
If your heart is with the camels and goats, don't come with me.

97
00:07:48,298 --> 00:07:51,185
He's not looking for numbers; he could gather a crowd and take them to war.

98
00:07:51,205 --> 00:07:52,369
He said; No! I don't want you.

99
00:07:52,515 --> 00:07:57,689
This battle needs people who have, Ikhlas(اِخْلَاص); who have sincerity.

100
00:07:58,789 --> 00:08:02,513
If you're coming, and doing this half-heartedly; stay home.

101
00:08:03,173 --> 00:08:05,147
And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

102
00:08:05,547 --> 00:08:11,227
فغزا ، فأدنَى من لقريةِ حين صلاةِ العصرِ ، أو قريبًا من ذلك ،

103
00:08:11,414 --> 00:08:15,353
 فقال للشَّمسِ : أنت مأمورةٌ وأنا مأمورٌ ،

104
00:08:15,466 --> 00:08:21,460
اللَّهمَّ احبِسْها عليَّ شيئًا ، فحُبِست عليه ، حتَّى فتح اللهُ عليه ،

105
00:08:21,833 --> 00:08:25,834
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; He fought; until it was time of Asr(عصر),

106
00:08:26,221 --> 00:08:30,830
and then he told the sun; you are receiving orders, and I'm receiving orders, oh Allah! Stop the sun.

107
00:08:31,037 --> 00:08:36,493
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى stop the sun, until he achieved victory, and he won.

108
00:08:37,924 --> 00:08:41,684
This is the story of Sayidina Yusha Bin Noon(سيدنا يوشع بن نون).

109
00:08:42,244 --> 00:08:49,566
They won, and they entered into Jerusalem, and they started expanding their nation; under the banner of;

110
00:08:49,606 --> 00:08:50,735
لا إلهَ إلاَّ اللَّه

111
00:08:51,228 --> 00:08:57,731
Time past; few generations, maybe a few centuries, and then the enemies were regrouping and attacking again.

112
00:08:57,951 --> 00:09:01,591
And there was a continuous Jihad(جهاد) with Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

113
00:09:02,304 --> 00:09:04,430
Under the leadership of one of their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء);

114
00:09:05,037 --> 00:09:08,690
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) came to their Nabi(نَبِي), and they told him;

115
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:15,022
Send us a king; so that we can fight under his leadership.

116
00:09:16,682 --> 00:09:18,029
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

117
00:09:18,092 --> 00:09:36,761
أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ مِن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ مِن بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ إِذْ قَالُوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَّهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا

118
00:09:37,228 --> 00:09:42,122
Have you not thought about the group of the children of Israel(اسرائيل) after the time of Musa(موسى),

119
00:09:42,356 --> 00:09:49,491
when they said to a prophet of theirs; appoint for us a king and we will fight in Allah's way?

120
00:09:50,411 --> 00:09:55,455
They came to their Nabi(نَبِي), and they told them; We want to fight in the sake of Allah.

121
00:09:55,989 --> 00:09:57,629
Their Nabi(نَبِي) was very wise.

122
00:09:58,135 --> 00:10:02,711
قَالَ هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِن كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ أَلَّا تُقَاتِلُوا ۖ

123
00:10:03,651 --> 00:10:08,802
He said; Would you then refrain from fighting, when fighting was prescribed for you?

124
00:10:09,055 --> 00:10:14,059
He said; You're asking for fighting; but when fighting is prescribed on you, will you fight?

125
00:10:14,899 --> 00:10:18,945
Because it's easy to claim, that you're willing to fight.

126
00:10:19,292 --> 00:10:23,835
And people talk, but rarely do we find anybody walking the talk?

127
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:34,913
People say that; We're willing to fight in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and they're giving out these sermons, and everybody is motivated and encouraged.

128
00:10:34,933 --> 00:10:39,366
But then, when it comes to the real situation; people back out.

129
00:10:40,359 --> 00:10:47,202
And the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told them, he said; Now you're asking for fighting; what if it is prescribed on you, Will you then fight?

130
00:10:48,249 --> 00:10:49,436
They said; Definitely!

131
00:10:49,662 --> 00:10:54,794
وَمَا لَنَا أَلَّا نُقَاتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَقَدْ أُخْرِجْنَا مِن دِيَارِنَا وَأَبْنَائِنَا ۖ

132
00:10:55,114 --> 00:11:01,321
Why shouldn't we fight in the sake of Allah, when we have been driven out of our homes and our children.

133
00:11:01,774 --> 00:11:04,754
They have kicked us out of our land; how come we will not fight?

134
00:11:04,928 --> 00:11:07,447
And we will fight in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

135
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:13,331
And they gave their promises, and they said; We will fight in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; Don't worry! We will fight.

136
00:11:14,011 --> 00:11:14,877
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

137
00:11:14,917 --> 00:11:19,086
فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوْا إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّنْهُمْ ۗ

138
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:24,567
But when fighting was ordered for them, they turned away; all except a few of them.

139
00:11:24,667 --> 00:11:30,466
We should never be fooled by the claims that we hear, and the talk.

140
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:36,705
Because talk is free, It doesn't cost you anything to talk; but fighting in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى cost you a lot.

141
00:11:37,599 --> 00:11:40,572
You can make a claim that you will open Jerusalem if you want.

142
00:11:41,019 --> 00:11:49,019
Talking big is easy, but the sacrifice and especially long term sacrifice which he had needs, that is difficult.

143
00:11:49,892 --> 00:11:55,253
Jihad(جهاد) is not only sacrifice, but it's a long term sacrifice and that is, where people fail.

144
00:11:55,726 --> 00:12:01,698
If you are asked to sacrifice in one time; you could be fired up with a speech

145
00:12:01,758 --> 00:12:06,557
and then you would give out your money for example; and you would sacrifice, that could happen.

146
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:15,006
But when you're asked to sacrifice for a long period; and you're suffering hardship for a long time; that is what causes people to fail.

147
00:12:16,012 --> 00:12:17,899
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they said;

148
00:12:17,919 --> 00:12:23,424
We're gonna fight; why shouldn't we fight, and we were driven out of our homes and driven out of our children?

149
00:12:23,737 --> 00:12:26,237
When Allahسُبحانه وتعالى prescribed fighting on them, they didn't.

150
00:12:27,197 --> 00:12:31,779
But now, it's too late to back out, because the orders are the revealed.

151
00:12:33,152 --> 00:12:37,257
They asked for a king, they asked for a leader; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with one.

152
00:12:37,844 --> 00:12:38,944
Their Nabi(نَبِي) said;

153
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:48,133
وَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ طَالُوتَ مَلِكًا ۚ

154
00:12:48,456 --> 00:12:53,221
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has sent to you Talut(طالوت) as a king.

155
00:12:53,681 --> 00:12:56,761
Allah has appointed for you a king, and he is Talut(طالوت).

156
00:12:56,928 --> 00:13:02,803
Now, these people who asked to fight in the sake of Allah; they were the first one to argue with the commandment of their Nabi(نَبِي).

157
00:13:02,917 --> 00:13:05,906
They came to the Nabi(نَبِي), and they said; We want a leader,

158
00:13:05,926 --> 00:13:09,912
when they were provided with a leader; they started arguing and they said; We don't want it.

159
00:13:10,265 --> 00:13:17,151
They are asking for a king, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided them with the leader, and then they said; We don't want him.

160
00:13:17,281 --> 00:13:17,988
Why?

161
00:13:18,468 --> 00:13:19,688
They gave two reasons.

162
00:13:20,628 --> 00:13:25,820
They gave two reasons; why they disagree with the appointment of Talut(طالوت) as a king.

163
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:41,893
قَالُوا أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنَا وَنَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِالْمُلْكِ مِنْهُ وَلَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِّنَ الْمَالِ ۚ

164
00:13:42,126 --> 00:13:42,646
Two reasons:

165
00:13:42,666 --> 00:13:45,133
Number one; He's not from the nobility;

166
00:13:45,606 --> 00:13:47,075
he's not from the noble families.

167
00:13:47,795 --> 00:13:49,542
Number two; He's not wealthy.

168
00:13:49,842 --> 00:13:51,029
These are the two reasons.

169
00:13:51,935 --> 00:13:56,434
How can he be a king, when he does not belong to the high class?

170
00:13:57,734 --> 00:14:01,180
And how can he be a king when he is not wealthy?

171
00:14:03,293 --> 00:14:12,704
And this is the nature of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); what they consider to be success in life; is the status of which class you come from,

172
00:14:12,944 --> 00:14:15,444
because they always use race as an issue.

173
00:14:15,718 --> 00:14:20,673
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the Jews, it's an issue to them; We are the chosen people, we are the special people,

174
00:14:20,909 --> 00:14:23,459
you are the Gentiles, you are lower class.

175
00:14:23,683 --> 00:14:25,463
So race is important to them.

176
00:14:25,743 --> 00:14:27,416
And then the second issue of money.

177
00:14:29,136 --> 00:14:33,835
These are the criteria that they use; race and money.

178
00:14:34,702 --> 00:14:39,587
And this is a disease that is in the hearts of the children of Israel(اسرائيل); Al-Yahood(ال يهود),

179
00:14:39,727 --> 00:14:44,351
and it's also a disease that exists somewhat among us.

180
00:14:44,945 --> 00:14:49,611
We consider people to be successful, according to how much money they have.

181
00:14:50,645 --> 00:14:51,704
What did they say?

182
00:14:52,344 --> 00:14:53,517
How much is he, what?

183
00:14:53,737 --> 00:14:54,364
Worth.

184
00:14:55,004 --> 00:14:56,211
How much is he worth?

185
00:14:57,351 --> 00:15:00,893
So we qualify the person according to how much Money he has.

186
00:15:01,486 --> 00:15:03,220
When you say, how much the person is worth?

187
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:03,986
What you're talking about?

188
00:15:04,006 --> 00:15:04,626
His money;

189
00:15:05,026 --> 00:15:06,986
he is worth a billion, he is worth a million.

190
00:15:07,199 --> 00:15:09,148
If he doesn't have any money; he's worth nothing.

191
00:15:10,135 --> 00:15:11,448
His Eeman(ايمان) doesn't matter?

192
00:15:11,695 --> 00:15:12,915
His Salah(صلوة) doesn't matter?

193
00:15:13,055 --> 00:15:14,295
His Deen(دِيْن) doesn't matter?

194
00:15:14,461 --> 00:15:17,320
If he doesn't have any money; he is worth nothing.

195
00:15:18,833 --> 00:15:21,746
Their Nabi(نَبِي) is teaching them that, this is wrong; he told them;

196
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,893
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفَاهُ عَلَيْكُمْ

197
00:15:23,933 --> 00:15:26,440
Allah has chosen him among you; That's it.

198
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,852
This is enough to settle the argument; Allah is the one who chose him.

199
00:15:30,545 --> 00:15:39,374
Don't argue! His ancestry, his ethnicity, his race, doesn't matter, his wealth doesn't matter.

200
00:15:39,399 --> 00:15:39,700
Why?

201
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,660
Allah has chosen him.

202
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:43,898
So that could have been the end of the conversation.

203
00:15:44,678 --> 00:15:46,291
Allah has chosen him, peri.

204
00:15:46,838 --> 00:15:51,879
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to teach us; how to choose leaders?

205
00:15:53,312 --> 00:15:59,604
Therefore, the Nabi(نَبِي) has told them two qualifications you should be looking for; when you're looking for a leader.

206
00:16:00,724 --> 00:16:02,864
They gave two reasons why he shouldn't be a leader;

207
00:16:03,058 --> 00:16:05,931
their Nabi(نَبِي) gave them two reasons why he should be the leader.

208
00:16:07,864 --> 00:16:08,568
He said;

209
00:16:09,033 --> 00:16:18,623
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفَاهُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَزَادَهُ بَسْطَةً فِي الْعِلْمِ وَالْجِسْمِ ۖ

210
00:16:19,023 --> 00:16:25,176
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has increased him amply in two things; knowledge and strength.

211
00:16:25,853 --> 00:16:29,400
Allah has given him two things; knowledge and strength.

212
00:16:30,173 --> 00:16:37,274
The word knowledge is defined according to the job, which you are appointing the leader to.

213
00:16:38,314 --> 00:16:39,322
Why am I saying this?

214
00:16:39,388 --> 00:16:44,648
Because many times whenever we say knowledge; our minds would immediately take us to Fiqh(فقه)

215
00:16:45,521 --> 00:16:47,228
and that's not necessarily in the case.

216
00:16:47,828 --> 00:16:56,593
If a person is going to be appointed as a military leader, then he should have a lot of knowledge in fighting; in war.

217
00:16:56,913 --> 00:17:01,700
And that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to be the general; the Ameer(أمير) of the army,

218
00:17:02,326 --> 00:17:04,912
but it wasn't Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was appointed to be the Khalifah(خليفه).

219
00:17:05,612 --> 00:17:07,772
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was appointed to be the Khalifah(خليفه).

220
00:17:08,106 --> 00:17:11,916
Every position has its knowledge that is required.

221
00:17:12,801 --> 00:17:20,292
Talut(طالوت) had the knowledge, he needed for the job of leading Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) in Jihad(جهاد), and he had strength.

222
00:17:20,578 --> 00:17:23,572
And again, strength is defined according to the job.

223
00:17:23,785 --> 00:17:25,525
It's not a matter of physical strength.

224
00:17:25,805 --> 00:17:28,025
You don't need to have a body builder for every job.

225
00:17:28,485 --> 00:17:31,351
In this job, you need to be physically strong.

226
00:17:32,484 --> 00:17:42,051
But in other types of jobs that needs to have mental strength, or strength of wealth, or strength of heart, it depends on the type of job.

227
00:17:42,291 --> 00:17:47,056
But these are the two things; you should look for in the leader; knowledge and strength.

228
00:17:47,143 --> 00:17:49,036
وَزَادَهُ بَسْطَةً فِي الْعِلْمِ وَالْجسْد

229
00:17:49,875 --> 00:17:50,375
Then he said;

230
00:17:50,395 --> 00:17:51,995
وَاللَّهُ يُؤْتِي مُلْكَهُ مَن يَشَاءُ ۚ

231
00:17:52,015 --> 00:17:54,813
Allah gives the kingdom to whomever He wills.

232
00:17:55,086 --> 00:17:57,499
It's not up to you; it's up to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

233
00:17:57,893 --> 00:18:14,345
وَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ ءَايَةَ مُلْكِهِۦٓ أَن يَأْتِيَكُمُ ٱلتَّابُوتُ فِيهِ سَكِينَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَبَقِيَّةٌ

234
00:18:15,186 --> 00:18:27,226
وَبَقِيَّةٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ ءَالُ مُوسَىٰ وَءَالُ هَٰرُونَ تَحْمِلُهُ ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ ۚ

235
00:18:27,913 --> 00:18:40,064
إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةً لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ۝

236
00:18:40,371 --> 00:18:46,808
Allah to strengthen their hearts is going to appoint; Talut(طالوت) as a king through a ceremony,

237
00:18:46,988 --> 00:18:54,051
and this ceremony would be a miracle from Allah; to strengthen their hearts so that they would accept him as a leader.

238
00:18:54,211 --> 00:18:56,669
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is gonna provide a miracle; Ayah(آية).

239
00:18:57,043 --> 00:18:59,369
That Ayah(آية) was At-Taboot(التَّابُوت).

240
00:18:59,749 --> 00:19:01,882
At-Taboot(التَّابُوت) is a casket.

241
00:19:02,055 --> 00:19:06,942
In that casket, were some of the belongings of Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون).

242
00:19:07,022 --> 00:19:11,791
And Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) used to consider that to be Barakah(بركة), because it is left behind from the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

243
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:16,169
And between them and Musa(موسى) are centuries; few hundreds of years.

244
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:20,882
So they have been separated from Musa(موسى) through a long history.

245
00:19:21,309 --> 00:19:29,253
They had some of the belongings of Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون) in a casket, and they used to consider that to be Barakah(بركة) for them,

246
00:19:29,446 --> 00:19:32,426
because it's left behind from the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

247
00:19:32,599 --> 00:19:35,923
What happened is; the enemy was able to take hold of this.

248
00:19:36,503 --> 00:19:38,143
And the enemy took it away from them.

249
00:19:38,330 --> 00:19:41,995
This Ayah(آية); Miracle that Allah has gonna give them is that;

250
00:19:42,208 --> 00:19:47,770
this Tabut(تابوت); casket will be delivered by the angels to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

251
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:53,060
So the angels carried this casket, and brought it back to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

252
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:58,280
And in it; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also says is; Sakinah(سكينة); Tranquility; peace for you.

253
00:19:58,513 --> 00:20:02,665
This belongs to the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); Allah will bring it back to you. So it's gonna be Sakinah(سكينة) for you.

254
00:20:03,918 --> 00:20:06,191
Talut(طالوت) was appointed as a king.

255
00:20:07,284 --> 00:20:09,770
فَلَمَّا فَصَلَ طَالُوتُ بِالْجُنُودِ

256
00:20:10,650 --> 00:20:14,506
When Talut(طالوت) set out with the army.

257
00:20:15,439 --> 00:20:24,058
Talut(طالوت) now, recruited all of the men, and he set out with them; Fasala(فَصَلَ)

258
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:26,789
فَلَمَّا فَصَلَ طَالُوتُ بِالْجُنُودِ

259
00:20:26,815 --> 00:20:30,115
Meaning; that he separated himself from the rest of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

260
00:20:30,249 --> 00:20:35,938
All of the children, and the women, and the elderly are left behind and now, Talut(طالوت) is with the; fighters.

261
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:37,518
He has the soldiers with him.

262
00:20:38,144 --> 00:20:42,258
As-Suddi(السدى); one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) says; they numbered 80,000.

263
00:20:42,718 --> 00:20:46,704
His army was 80,000 soldiers; men.

264
00:20:47,607 --> 00:20:49,433
Talut(طالوت) is not looking for numbers.

265
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:55,796
Talut(طالوت) knows that what he is facing ahead; needs an iron will.

266
00:20:56,782 --> 00:20:59,562
It needs patience, it needs strength.

267
00:20:59,956 --> 00:21:06,578
Therefore, he's gonna take his ummah(امة); he is gonna take this army, through a series of tests.

268
00:21:08,231 --> 00:21:09,698
He's not gonna take them and fight.

269
00:21:09,718 --> 00:21:11,471
He's not looking for a crowd.

270
00:21:12,538 --> 00:21:16,273
He's looking for strong soldiers who can fight with him.

271
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:27,154
Because Talut(طالوت); out of his wisdom knew; that if there are any weak soldiers with us, they're gonna cause us more harm than benefit.

272
00:21:28,081 --> 00:21:30,992
And we know that from the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

273
00:21:31,759 --> 00:21:40,216
In the Battle of the Tabook(تبوك); the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) were coming Rasool Allah ﷺ, and everyone was giving an excuse to stay behind.

274
00:21:41,470 --> 00:21:44,032
 I mean, they were inventing excuses.

275
00:21:44,065 --> 00:21:48,905
One of them even came and said; Oh Rasool Allah ﷺ! I fear the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of woman.

276
00:21:49,185 --> 00:21:53,747
I don't wanna go with you and fight because, if I see women then, I would lose my mind.

277
00:21:54,027 --> 00:21:55,621
That is the excuse that he gave.

278
00:21:55,661 --> 00:21:57,219
He said; Please let me stay here!

279
00:21:58,379 --> 00:22:01,353
Munafiqeen(مُنافقين); they were coming to Rasool Allah ﷺ and everyone was giving an excuse.

280
00:22:01,846 --> 00:22:05,198
And Rasool Allah ﷺ knows that they are Munafiqeen(مُنافقين), and he is telling them; stay behind.

281
00:22:05,772 --> 00:22:07,278
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

282
00:22:07,878 --> 00:22:10,624
وَلَوْ أَرَادُوا الْخُرُوجَ لَأَعَدُّوا لَهُ عُدَّةً

283
00:22:10,997 --> 00:22:16,424
If they were serious that they wanted to fight, they would have found ways to prepare for it.

284
00:22:17,211 --> 00:22:21,637
But they're not serious, they don't want to fight, these excuses are fake.

285
00:22:22,477 --> 00:22:27,326
If they were serious; if they were true in their intentions to fight;

286
00:22:27,453 --> 00:22:28,273
لَأَعَدُّوا لَهُ عُدَّةً

287
00:22:28,293 --> 00:22:29,553
They would have prepared for it.

288
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:32,702
Now, they're waiting till the last moment and then, they're coming and saying;

289
00:22:32,722 --> 00:22:35,395
I have business that is not done yet.

290
00:22:35,668 --> 00:22:36,169
Allah is saying;

291
00:22:36,189 --> 00:22:38,022
وَلَوْ أَرَادُوا الْخُرُوجَ لَأَعَدُّوا لَهُ عُدَّةً

292
00:22:38,042 --> 00:22:40,572
If they were serious, they would have prepared for it early.

293
00:22:41,032 --> 00:22:42,705
And they would have been able to go.

294
00:22:43,258 --> 00:22:47,697
وَلَٰكِن كَرِهَ اللَّهُ انبِعَاثَهُمْ فَثَبَّطَهُمْ وَقِيلَ اقْعُدُوا مَعَ الْقَاعِدِينَ۝

295
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:50,024
Allah did not want them to go out.

296
00:22:50,404 --> 00:22:52,573
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them stay behind.

297
00:22:53,633 --> 00:22:56,735
Allah does not want them to go out with his Nabi(نَبِي);

298
00:22:57,048 --> 00:22:58,095
why?

299
00:22:58,968 --> 00:23:00,175
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

300
00:23:00,228 --> 00:23:03,388
لَوْ خَرَجُواْ فِيكُم مَّا زَادُوكُمْ إِلَّا خَبَالًا

301
00:23:03,528 --> 00:23:07,774
If they went out with you, they would have cost you nothing but weakness.

302
00:23:08,568 --> 00:23:13,980
These soldiers; if they come out with you, oh Muhammadﷺ! They gonna cause you weakness.

303
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:19,095
Because when the battle starts, and the screws are tightened, then they gonna fail.

304
00:23:19,795 --> 00:23:25,624
So instead of having a brother next to your side helping you in the battlefield; you're gonna have somebody who is putting fear in your heart,

305
00:23:25,644 --> 00:23:26,810
telling you; Let's run away!

306
00:23:27,264 --> 00:23:28,680
Therefore, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

307
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:29,393
فَثَبَّطَهُمْ

308
00:23:29,413 --> 00:23:33,852
Allah did not want them to go out, and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them stay behind.

309
00:23:33,952 --> 00:23:36,945
Because if they went with you, they would cause you nothing but weakness;

310
00:23:37,012 --> 00:23:37,592
خَبَالًا

311
00:23:37,825 --> 00:23:40,571
Talut(طالوت) did not want this quality of people to come with him.

312
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:42,097
He did not want them in his army.

313
00:23:42,757 --> 00:23:47,776
And we know in the Battle of Hunayn(حنين); because there were many new Muslims in the army,

314
00:23:48,056 --> 00:23:51,303
after Fath Makkah(فتح مكه), there were many who just became Muslim.

315
00:23:51,643 --> 00:23:59,508
When Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah(مكه), that was the hugest army ever that's Rasool Allah ﷺ had.

316
00:24:00,328 --> 00:24:02,366
And one of the Sahabah(صحابه) looked at this army and said;

317
00:24:02,406 --> 00:24:06,282
لن نغلب الیوم القلۃ

318
00:24:06,301 --> 00:24:08,141
We're not going to lose because of numbers.

319
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:10,335
Numbers is not going to be factored in this war.

320
00:24:10,361 --> 00:24:11,781
Look at this huge number we have.

321
00:24:11,955 --> 00:24:13,474
What happened in the Battle of Hunayn(حنين)?

322
00:24:13,727 --> 00:24:18,516
As soon as they received the first blow from the enemy; they were running in every direction.

323
00:24:19,562 --> 00:24:21,069
They were running in every direction.

324
00:24:21,542 --> 00:24:23,449
Talut(طالوت) didn't want these with him.

325
00:24:23,842 --> 00:24:25,829
So he's going to take them through a test.

326
00:24:26,362 --> 00:24:27,162
This test is;

327
00:24:27,182 --> 00:24:28,647
إِنَّ اللَّهَ مُبْتَلِيكُم بِنَهَرٍ

328
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:30,160
Allah is going to test you with a river.

329
00:24:30,547 --> 00:24:33,894
Talut(طالوت) made them march; in the desert.

330
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:38,811
And he made them thirsty, exhausted and tired.

331
00:24:39,698 --> 00:24:43,247
And then when they saw water in front of their eyes;

332
00:24:43,401 --> 00:24:44,454
Talut(طالوت) said; Don't drink!

333
00:24:45,094 --> 00:24:47,412
Thirsty, exhausted, tired.

334
00:24:49,145 --> 00:24:53,035
Some of them are maybe wondering that we might face death, if we don't drink.

335
00:24:53,475 --> 00:24:54,955
Talut(طالوت) said; Don't drink!

336
00:24:55,528 --> 00:24:57,394
مَن شَرِبَ مِنْهُ فَلَيْسَ مِنِّي

337
00:24:57,414 --> 00:25:01,168
Whoever drinks, does not belong to me, you cannot come with me anymore.

338
00:25:02,155 --> 00:25:04,241
وَمَن لَّمْ يَطْعَمْهُ فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي

339
00:25:04,454 --> 00:25:06,568
And if you do not drink, then you can come with me.

340
00:25:06,801 --> 00:25:08,508
إِلَّا مَنِ اغْتَرَفَ غُرْفَةً بِيَدِهِ ۚ

341
00:25:08,641 --> 00:25:11,650
Or if you drink one handful, then you can still come with me.

342
00:25:12,036 --> 00:25:13,569
So you either don't drink;

343
00:25:13,796 --> 00:25:20,577
or if you drink you only drink one handful; just one hand, and one hand cannot take much; not two hands, one hand.

344
00:25:21,551 --> 00:25:25,509
I assume that; it is easier not to drink, rather than take one drink.

345
00:25:26,176 --> 00:25:33,561
Because when you take that first drink; Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is going to make it taste, the best sip of water that you ever had in your life.

346
00:25:34,541 --> 00:25:41,560
And in the end, the result was 80,000 went through this admission test.

347
00:25:42,567 --> 00:25:50,377
And only 4000 graduated, out of 80,000 76,000 of them drank from the river.

348
00:25:51,417 --> 00:25:54,154
Only 4000 crossed it to the other side.

349
00:25:54,448 --> 00:25:57,534
The rest failed from the first test.

350
00:25:57,808 --> 00:26:00,614
76,000 were left Behind.

351
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:02,247
Talut(طالوت) is not looking for numbers.

352
00:26:02,334 --> 00:26:04,134
These are men who are willing to go and fight with him.

353
00:26:04,154 --> 00:26:06,409
He said; Don't come with me! You're not allowed.

354
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:08,843
It's a test of will.

355
00:26:09,543 --> 00:26:15,969
Because he wants to have men with him, who are willing to stand up; against temptations,

356
00:26:16,622 --> 00:26:21,394
and who are going to be patient against hardship.

357
00:26:22,127 --> 00:26:25,087
They're willing to stand up against the strong temptations.

358
00:26:26,134 --> 00:26:30,775
And in the same time, they are very patient and enduring hardship.

359
00:26:31,942 --> 00:26:33,894
In the end, 4000 remained with him.

360
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:42,423
When they cross to the other side of the river; and the ones who are left behind with Talut(طالوت) were only 4000.

361
00:26:42,836 --> 00:26:45,143
Then that was another test for them.

362
00:26:45,450 --> 00:26:46,983
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

363
00:26:47,283 --> 00:26:58,689
فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَهُ هُوَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ قَالُوا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا الْيَوْمَ بِجَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ ۚ

364
00:26:59,242 --> 00:27:02,869
They said; We have no way of fighting Jalut(جالوت).

365
00:27:03,842 --> 00:27:06,362
 4000; do you want us to fight Jalut(جالوت), look at his army?

366
00:27:06,575 --> 00:27:07,437
There's no way!

367
00:27:08,057 --> 00:27:09,137
The believers;

368
00:27:09,897 --> 00:27:12,667
قَالَ الَّذِينَ يَظُنُّونَ أَنَّهُم مُّلَاقُو اللَّهِ

369
00:27:12,727 --> 00:27:17,699
The ones; who are sure, that they are going to meet Allah, they said;

370
00:27:17,872 --> 00:27:21,212
كَم مِّن فِئَةٍ قَلِيلَةٍ غَلَبَتْ فِئَةً كَثِيرَةً بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۗ

371
00:27:21,386 --> 00:27:26,836
How many times; has a small group defeated a larger group; with the will of Allah?

372
00:27:26,981 --> 00:27:30,041
It's not a matter of numbers, who are these we're speaking?

373
00:27:30,115 --> 00:27:32,367
The ones who are sure that, they will meet Allah.

374
00:27:32,553 --> 00:27:37,939
So, they're not thinking in terms of this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); but they're thinking in terms of meeting Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

375
00:27:38,139 --> 00:27:39,412
The others are telling them;

376
00:27:39,499 --> 00:27:45,924
No, let's be real! Let's be real! 4000 against this huge army; there is no way we can win.

377
00:27:46,237 --> 00:27:49,077
They're thinking in terms of the logic of this world.

378
00:27:49,464 --> 00:27:50,670
What they can see with their eyes?

379
00:27:50,710 --> 00:27:54,463
I can see with my eyes; the larger army, they can defeat us.

380
00:27:54,973 --> 00:27:56,472
They're not believing in the unseen.

381
00:27:57,612 --> 00:27:59,738
So now, another group failed.

382
00:28:01,005 --> 00:28:07,284
In the end, Talut(طالوت) was left with the pure; the best of the children of Israel(اسرائيل);

383
00:28:08,064 --> 00:28:15,283
314; Out of 80,000; 314 remained with Talut(طالوت).

384
00:28:15,877 --> 00:28:19,181
The Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, it is narrated that, they said;

385
00:28:19,388 --> 00:28:32,526
We were told that, the number of Mujahideen(مجاهدين) or fighters, which were with Talut(طالوت); was the same number as the ones who fought in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

386
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:34,931
 ثلاثمائة وعشرة

387
00:28:35,384 --> 00:28:36,644
More than, 310.

388
00:28:36,917 --> 00:28:40,818
These are the ones, who remained with Talut(طالوت); out of 80,000.

389
00:28:42,144 --> 00:28:47,023
Talut(طالوت) took them through test; that would separate between the men and the boys; set them aside.

390
00:28:47,723 --> 00:28:50,949
He take the strong in one side, and the weak and the unfit on the other side.

391
00:28:50,969 --> 00:28:56,748
In the end he was left with 310 or 314.

392
00:28:57,115 --> 00:29:01,959
These 314 Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about them;

393
00:29:02,559 --> 00:29:05,092
وَلَمَّا بَرَزُوا لِجَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ

394
00:29:05,239 --> 00:29:06,368
And when they faced

395
00:29:06,475 --> 00:29:07,821
جَالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ

396
00:29:08,061 --> 00:29:17,127
Before that, Talut(طالوت) was taking them through tests, to see; how patient they are, how strong they are, how determined are they?

397
00:29:17,774 --> 00:29:23,532
But now, when they are facing the enemy; he is putting all of that aside.

398
00:29:24,045 --> 00:29:28,680
It's not your strength, it is not your patience, it is not your will.

399
00:29:29,020 --> 00:29:33,913
All of these are means; now it is pending on Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

400
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:36,412
So we use the means before.

401
00:29:36,772 --> 00:29:40,019
These means; you prepare for them before the battle.

402
00:29:40,372 --> 00:29:45,878
But then when you are in the battlefield; you do not depend on the means anymore.

403
00:29:46,124 --> 00:29:47,744
You depend on Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

404
00:29:48,111 --> 00:29:53,276
Rasool Allah ﷺ lined up the army; gave them instructions and orders in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

405
00:29:53,390 --> 00:29:55,763
But then when it was time to fighting; what did Rasool Allah ﷺ do?

406
00:29:56,063 --> 00:29:58,036
He went on a hilltop and started making Dua(دُعَا).

407
00:29:58,563 --> 00:30:02,396
Now, you put your whole dependency on Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

408
00:30:03,449 --> 00:30:07,828
At that moment, when they were facing Jalut(جالوت); what did they say?

409
00:30:07,921 --> 00:30:10,315
قَالُوا رَبَّنَا أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا

410
00:30:10,335 --> 00:30:16,534
Now they are directing their call to Allah; Oh Allah! Shower us or cover us with patience,

411
00:30:16,574 --> 00:30:17,420
Allahu Akbar(الله اكبر)!

412
00:30:17,560 --> 00:30:19,758
They're not asking for patience; they're saying;

413
00:30:19,798 --> 00:30:21,118
أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا

414
00:30:21,298 --> 00:30:23,211
Oh Allah! Cover us with patience.

415
00:30:23,505 --> 00:30:25,525
Because, you don't need a little bit of patience.

416
00:30:25,778 --> 00:30:28,858
You do not need a small amount; you need a lot.

417
00:30:29,418 --> 00:30:29,811
So they said;

418
00:30:29,865 --> 00:30:30,504
أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا

419
00:30:30,529 --> 00:30:34,499
Afrigh(أَفْرِغْ) is like; you have big bucket, and you're pouring it over someone.

420
00:30:34,539 --> 00:30:35,666
That is; Ifraagh(اِفرَاغ).

421
00:30:36,359 --> 00:30:37,512
أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا

422
00:30:37,606 --> 00:30:39,201
Pour on us patience.

423
00:30:39,668 --> 00:30:40,774
وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدَامَنَا

424
00:30:40,974 --> 00:30:43,014
And make our feet firm.

425
00:30:43,894 --> 00:30:45,435
وَٱنصُرْنَا عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ۝

426
00:30:45,549 --> 00:30:47,615
And give us victory over the nonbelievers.

427
00:30:48,522 --> 00:30:49,530
The battle started.

428
00:30:50,170 --> 00:30:53,117
A huge army was fighting the small army.

429
00:30:53,137 --> 00:30:54,610
فِئَةٍ قَلِيلَةٍ وَالطَّالُوت

430
00:30:55,557 --> 00:30:58,860
Jalut(جالوت) was the king of the enemy;

431
00:30:59,333 --> 00:31:08,701
powerful, huge, strong man with arrogance and pride; fighting in the battlefield; asking for anyone to challenge him.

432
00:31:09,174 --> 00:31:10,654
Who dares to fight me?

433
00:31:11,587 --> 00:31:17,548
Talut(طالوت) said; Who will go out and get rid of him; who will eliminate Jalut(جالوت)?

434
00:31:18,922 --> 00:31:20,810
He didn't get any response.

435
00:31:21,237 --> 00:31:23,449
A young man; short.

436
00:31:24,063 --> 00:31:29,955
He was described by; Wahb Ibn Munabieh(وھب ابن منبہ) As a short man came up to Talut(طالوت) and said; I will!

437
00:31:30,268 --> 00:31:36,761
Talut(طالوت) saw that this is a child; so he made the announcement again; Who will go and face Jalut(جالوت)?

438
00:31:37,954 --> 00:31:40,146
Nobody responded except this young man.

439
00:31:40,733 --> 00:31:43,439
And for the third time; nobody came except him.

440
00:31:43,693 --> 00:31:45,141
Talut(طالوت) said; Then go!

441
00:31:46,494 --> 00:31:51,360
This young man was armed with a slingshot; with a slingshot.

442
00:31:51,793 --> 00:31:55,707
But he was armed with Eeman(ايمان) and trust in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in the heart.

443
00:31:56,567 --> 00:31:59,942
He went up to Jalut(جالوت) and challenged him.

444
00:32:00,276 --> 00:32:08,431
Jalut(جالوت) said; I don't want to fight you; you are a kid; send somebody stronger; I don't want to kill you.

445
00:32:08,544 --> 00:32:10,818
This young man said; But I want to kill you.

446
00:32:11,098 --> 00:32:18,859
And he put a small pebble in his slingshot, and he shot Jalut(جالوت), and Jalut(جالوت) was dead.

447
00:32:20,013 --> 00:32:22,621
He eliminated the king of the enemy.

448
00:32:23,048 --> 00:32:24,241
And the battle was over.

449
00:32:24,915 --> 00:32:28,188
And this young man was Dawoodعليه السلام.

450
00:32:29,855 --> 00:32:31,794
At that time, he was not a Nabi(نَبِي) yet.

451
00:32:32,101 --> 00:32:34,401
He was a young fighter in the army.

452
00:32:35,494 --> 00:32:41,573
After that, he was the one who inherited the kingdom from Talut(طالوت).

453
00:32:42,646 --> 00:32:52,019
And now, the children of Israel(اسرائيل) are going to enter into their golden age under the leadership of Dawoodعليه السلام and Sulaimanعليه السلام.

454
00:32:52,713 --> 00:32:58,838
But this was built on the shoulders of these 314 men who fought in that battle.

455
00:32:59,532 --> 00:33:05,452
Just like the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was established on the shoulders of the 300 and so who fought in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

456
00:33:06,711 --> 00:33:08,178
That is how you establish Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

457
00:33:08,871 --> 00:33:10,034
It's not by talking.

458
00:33:10,788 --> 00:33:12,494
He establish it by the sacrifice.

459
00:33:13,514 --> 00:33:18,007
And it's not an issue of numbers, but it's an issue of  men and strength in the hearts.

460
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:22,790
That is the best era; that Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) ever had.

461
00:33:23,070 --> 00:33:24,623
After that it was their downfall.

462
00:33:25,317 --> 00:33:29,675
After that it was the curse of their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) on them.

463
00:33:30,362 --> 00:33:38,070
It was their downfall; and it was the end until, they eventually were the nation whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was angry with.

464
00:33:39,357 --> 00:33:45,277
Even though; we are done with the story of Musa(موسى), but we're not done with the story of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

465
00:33:45,317 --> 00:33:49,819
and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) are going to continue with us until, we end the series of the lives of the prophets.

466
00:33:50,398 --> 00:33:53,589
Until the end of the series; we're still going to be talking about this ummah(امة)

467
00:33:53,609 --> 00:33:58,301
because every other Nabi(نَبِي) that we're going to talk about from now on, is from this nation; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

468
00:33:58,728 --> 00:34:02,946
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has made in the nation of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) and the nations of Al-Ulama(اَلعُلَمَا).

469
00:34:03,573 --> 00:34:09,589
Out of them were the best scholars of their age, and the best people of their time.

470
00:34:09,829 --> 00:34:14,496
It wasn't until, they neglected the book of Allah and throw it, behind their backs.

471
00:34:14,703 --> 00:34:18,727
That is when Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put his wrath and anger on them.

472
00:34:21,047 --> 00:34:22,347
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

473
00:34:22,387 --> 00:34:26,710
فَهَزَمُوهُم بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَقَتَلَ دَاوُودُ جَالُوتَ

474
00:34:27,923 --> 00:34:33,841
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; So they routed them by Allah's leave and David killed Goliath.

475
00:34:35,168 --> 00:34:39,925
وَآتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشَاءُ ۗ

476
00:34:40,685 --> 00:34:49,128
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And Allah gave him(David) the kingdom, after the death of Jalut(جالوت).

477
00:34:50,174 --> 00:34:51,880
وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشَاءُ ۗ

478
00:34:53,033 --> 00:34:56,478
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also taught him wisdom, and

479
00:34:56,518 --> 00:34:57,925
عَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشَاءُ ۗ

480
00:34:58,138 --> 00:35:01,621
And He taught him other things, that He will.

481
00:35:01,874 --> 00:35:09,669
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد), kingdom, and He has given him; Al-Hikmah(الحكمة); wisdom,

482
00:35:11,556 --> 00:35:14,252
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has taught him knowledge.

483
00:35:15,072 --> 00:35:24,310
Hikmah(حكمة) was interpreted as, good judgment, and the ability to run the affairs of the people.

484
00:35:26,597 --> 00:35:33,639
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) some miracles and unique qualities.

485
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:39,366
Dawoodعليه السلام; first of all, had a beautiful voice.

486
00:35:40,246 --> 00:35:50,134
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was hearing; Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(ابو موسى الاشعرى) who had the most beautiful voice among the Sahabah(صحابه) in recitation of Qur'an.

487
00:35:50,354 --> 00:35:53,621
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(ابو موسى الاشعرى) had the most beautiful voice in reading Qur'an.

488
00:35:54,567 --> 00:35:58,450
Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he heard him, read Qur'an, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

489
00:35:58,470 --> 00:36:01,083
لقد أوتيت مزمارا من مزامير آل داود

490
00:36:01,310 --> 00:36:05,685
You have been given a flute of the flutes of the family of Dawood(داؤد).

491
00:36:05,972 --> 00:36:10,491
This does not mean a flute, literally, it means the beauty of the sound.

492
00:36:11,131 --> 00:36:15,291
The sound was so beautiful, and Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(ابو موسى الاشعرى);

493
00:36:15,418 --> 00:36:17,490
You have part of that beautiful sound.

494
00:36:18,190 --> 00:36:28,627
Dawood(داؤد)'s voice was so beautiful; in his Tasbeeh(تسبيح) and reading of their Qur'an, which was their book; the book of Dawood(داؤد).

495
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:31,400
Because, Dawoodعليه السلام; he received the book from Allah.

496
00:36:31,740 --> 00:36:32,946
We know five books.

497
00:36:33,533 --> 00:36:39,198
There are many other messengers, who received books from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, but we know the names of five.

498
00:36:39,445 --> 00:36:42,146
 Al-Qur'an(القرآن); which was revealed on Muhammadﷺ.

499
00:36:42,893 --> 00:36:45,899
Al-Injeel(الانجيل); The Gospel; which was revealed on?

500
00:36:46,119 --> 00:36:47,439
Eesa(عيسى); Jesus.

501
00:36:47,915 --> 00:36:48,868
At-Torah(التورة)?

502
00:36:49,615 --> 00:36:51,961
The Torah(تورة); which was revealed on Musa(موسى).

503
00:36:52,366 --> 00:36:54,646
And then, Az-Zaboor(الزبور); which was revealed on?

504
00:36:55,092 --> 00:36:55,614
Dawood(داؤد).

505
00:36:55,734 --> 00:36:56,968
And then the final one was;

506
00:36:57,001 --> 00:36:58,028
Suhuf Ibrahim(صُحُف اِبْراهِيْم);

507
00:36:58,494 --> 00:37:01,194
The Scrolls; which were revealed to Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

508
00:37:02,021 --> 00:37:04,884
Dawood(داؤد) would recite; Az-Zaboor(الزبور).

509
00:37:05,824 --> 00:37:08,190
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made it so easy on him.

510
00:37:09,084 --> 00:37:17,926
When Sayidina Dawood(سيدناداؤد) would read Qur'an and make Dhikr(ذكر); the mountains and the birds would join with him, and they would repeat after him.

511
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:20,486
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

512
00:37:20,606 --> 00:37:26,585
وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ مِنَّا فَضْلًا ۖ

513
00:37:26,665 --> 00:37:31,354
يَا جِبَالُ أَوِّبِي مَعَهُ وَالطَّيْرَ ۖ

514
00:37:31,734 --> 00:37:34,061
Awwibi(أَوِّبِي) means; Tarji'ah(ترجيه); repeat after him.

515
00:37:34,081 --> 00:37:39,460
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is commanding the mountains and the birds to repeat after Dawood(داؤد).

516
00:37:40,367 --> 00:37:46,759
Imagine! Dawoodعليه السلام is reciting Qur'an, and the mountains and the birds are repeating after him.

517
00:37:47,645 --> 00:37:51,805
Because, everything around us is making Tasbeeh(تسبيح) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

518
00:37:52,438 --> 00:38:02,157
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Everything is making Tasbeeh(تسبيح); everything is glorifying Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; but you do not know, their glorifying.

519
00:38:03,104 --> 00:38:06,079
And what is the sound of lightning?

520
00:38:06,713 --> 00:38:07,333
Thunder?

521
00:38:07,599 --> 00:38:08,459
What is Thunder?

522
00:38:09,986 --> 00:38:11,353
Thunder is a Tasbeeh(تسبيح) of Allah.

523
00:38:11,486 --> 00:38:15,415
وَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ مِنْ خِيفَتِهِ

524
00:38:16,448 --> 00:38:19,288
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that; The thunder is making Tasbeeh(تسبيح).

525
00:38:19,875 --> 00:38:24,981
That sound of the thunder, is Tasbeeh(تسبيح) of Allah; is glorifying of Allah.

526
00:38:25,407 --> 00:38:28,330
Now tell this to a scientist; he's going to say,

527
00:38:28,350 --> 00:38:30,110
What is this nonsense that you're talking about?

528
00:38:30,157 --> 00:38:32,685
You don't know! Let me explain to you; what Thunder is?

529
00:38:33,312 --> 00:38:39,628
He will tell you that, Thunder is the sound waves that come from the lightning.

530
00:38:39,648 --> 00:38:47,828
When the lightning strikes, it causes a vacuum in the air, and that shock wave travels through the air,

531
00:38:48,035 --> 00:38:50,348
and that is; what you hear in the form of thunder.

532
00:38:50,595 --> 00:38:51,741
Well tell them; that is right!

533
00:38:52,481 --> 00:38:54,361
